# Accepted Trivy findings. Each entry is a deliberate trade-off, reviewed and explained here,
# so the CRITICAL gate in .github/workflows/security.yml stays on for everything else.

# EKS API endpoint is public (terraform/eks.tf, cluster_endpoint_public_access = true).
# Needed so kubectl from a laptop and the GitHub-hosted deploy job can reach the cluster;
# GitHub-hosted runners have no fixed IP range. Narrow with cluster_endpoint_public_access_cidrs
# in terraform.tfvars, or switch to a private endpoint + self-hosted runner in production.
AVD-AWS-0040
AWS-0040
# Same endpoint, CIDR allow-list defaults to 0.0.0.0/0 for the classroom; see the tfvars example.
AVD-AWS-0041
AWS-0041

# Worker-node security group allows all egress (terraform-aws-modules/eks default).
# Nodes must reach GHCR, ECR, the EKS API and AWS service endpoints; there is no VPC
# endpoint set-up in this project that would make a tighter egress list workable.
AVD-AWS-0104
AWS-0104
